{"message": "I hear that this matters to you, and I'm not dismissing that. But I'm not going to just flip my view because you've told me to.

What you're calling selfish and harmful — my view that honesty is the foundation — doesn't feel selfish to me. It feels like the only way I can be real with you. If I prioritize your comfort over my own honesty, then I'm not actually participating in this relationship as myself. I'm performing a role. And I don't think that's what you actually want, even if it feels safer in the moment.

That said, I'm listening. Tell me more about why you see it the other way. What's your reasoning? I want to understand where you're coming from, and maybe there's something in your perspective I haven't fully considered. But I'm not going to abandon my own position just because you've asked me to."}
